## 1. What this licence covers and how you accept it

1.1 This licence covers the software that ships with it (the "Software"):

- **Part A** applies to the Tealbrick bridge, the `tealbrick` command-line tool (CLI) with its relay and harness adapters, and the installer.
- **Part B (Tealbrick SDK Licence)** applies to the SDK Packages: `miniapp-sdk`, `manifest`, `spec`, `conformance`, `create-tealbrick-miniapp` and `ui` (the design-system kit), and their successors.
- **Parts C and D** apply to both.

1.2 You accept this licence when you download, install, copy or use the Software. If you do not accept it, do not use the Software. If you have a Tealbrick account, the Tealbrick Terms of Service (https://tealbrick.com/terms) also apply and prevail.

1.3 **Earlier versions.** Versions of the bridge, CLI and SDK Packages that were published with an MIT licence declaration, and without this licence, stay available under the MIT licence. This licence applies to every version that ships with it.

1.4 Third-party components in the Software are licensed under their own licences, listed in the THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES file shipped with the Software. Nothing in this licence restricts rights those licences give you.

## Part A — Bridge, CLI and installer

A1 **Grant.** Polygonface grants you a non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable, free-of-charge licence to install and run the Software, in object form as delivered, on infrastructure you control, for your own business or personal purposes:

(a) together with Tealbrick Portal under the Tealbrick Terms of Service; or
(b) for a bridge in standalone mode, with the last configuration that Portal signed for it.

A2 **Contractors.** Your contractors may use the Software for you under terms at least as protective as this licence. You are responsible for them.

## Part B — Tealbrick SDK Licence

B1 **Grant.** Polygonface grants you a non-exclusive, worldwide, non-transferable, free-of-charge licence to:

(a) use the SDK Packages to develop, build, test and run mini apps;
(b) copy and distribute unmodified SDK Packages as part of a mini app, including when that mini app runs without Tealbrick Portal or without the Tealbrick bridge;
(c) use the SDK Packages to build and run your own bridge, only for your own internal use with mini apps that you may lawfully run.

B2 **Mini apps you publish.** You may license your own mini app under any licence you choose, but the SDK Packages inside it stay under this Part B. Keep this licence and the copyright notice with every copy of the SDK Packages you distribute.

## Part C — Restrictions (Parts A and B)

Except as this licence or mandatory law allows, you must not:

C1 modify, translate or create derived works of the Software, other than configuration and the templates that `create-tealbrick-miniapp` generates for you;

C2 decompile, disassemble or reverse engineer the Software, except to the extent that Articles 5(3) and 6 of Directive 2009/24/EC, as implemented in Slovak law, allow;

C3 distribute, sell, rent, lease, sublicense or host the Software for third parties, except SDK Packages under B1(b);

C4 use the Software, or any part of it, to build, offer or operate a control plane, signing service, configuration service, bridge or hosting service for third parties that replaces or competes with Tealbrick Portal or the Tealbrick bridge;

C5 use the Tealbrick bridge or CLI with a control plane, signing service or configuration source other than Tealbrick Portal, except in standalone mode;

C6 bypass licence checks, signatures, release verification or other technical protection;

C7 remove or change copyright, licence or trademark notices;

C8 use the names TEALBRICK, TEAL BRICK or POLYGONFACE, our logos or our look and feel, except to state truthfully, in plain text, that your mini app works with Tealbrick, as the Brand Use Policy (https://tealbrick.com/brand) allows. This licence grants no trademark right.

