D4 **Liability.** Each sentence of this clause is independent.
(a) Nothing in this licence limits liability for intent, gross negligence, harm to life, body or health, liability under mandatory product liability law, or any other liability that mandatory law does not allow to limit. Items (b) to (d) do not apply to these cases.
(b) The Software is free of charge. Taking that into account, the parties agree that the highest loss Polygonface could foresee at the conclusion of this licence as a possible result of its breach (Slovak Commercial Code, § 379) is EUR 500.
(c) Separately, Polygonface's total liability under this licence is limited to EUR 500.
(d) Polygonface is not liable for the part of a loss that you caused or contributed to, or could have avoided, including by not installing a security update.
(e) If you also have a Tealbrick account, section 17 of the Terms of Service applies instead of (b) to (d).
(f) If you are a consumer, D3 and items (b) to (d) apply only as far as mandatory consumer protection law allows, and nothing in this licence limits your rights under that law.

D5 **Termination.** This licence ends automatically if you breach Part C and do not cure the breach within 15 days after Polygonface tells you of it. It ends at once, without a cure period, for a breach of C4, C5 or C6. Polygonface may also end Part A for an account that it terminated for breach under the Terms of Service. When the licence ends, stop using the Software and delete your copies, except copies of SDK Packages that you already distributed inside a mini app under B1(b), which stay licensed to their recipients.

D6 **Export and sanctions.** You must not use the Software in breach of EU or other applicable export control or sanctions law.

D7 **Governing law and courts.** Slovak law governs this licence, excluding its conflict-of-law rules and the UN Convention on Contracts for the International Sale of Goods. For business users, the competent court of the Slovak Republic determined by the registered office of Polygonface decides disputes, and Polygonface may also bring a claim in the courts of the EU Member State or Lugano Convention state where you have your seat. If you are a consumer, you keep the protection of the mandatory law of your country of habitual residence, you may sue in the courts of the Slovak Republic or of your country of domicile, and Polygonface may sue you only in the courts of your country of domicile.

